# Does the priest spell Heal, cast by the PLAYER himself, cure all nine
# non-PARALYSIS maladies its "and EA_HEALING" clauses name? Read by
# tools/check_heal_maladies.sh. bd inc-xr8i.
#
# THE NINE: BLIND, CONFUSED, DISEASED, STUNNED, POISONED, HALLU, BLEEDING,
# CHOKING, WOUNDED. PARALYSIS is deliberately out of scope (a separate,
# later design decision) and is never afflicted or checked here.
#
# THE ROUTE, in two halves.
#
#   Half one, AFFLICTION: tools/fixtures/heal-maladies-god.irh, spliced onto
#   a scratch copy of lib/main.irc by the check script (never onto the
#   tracked lib/), declares one test god. "Become Divine Champion" (wizard
#   mode) joins it and grants 30000 favour outright (src/Debug.cpp), which
#   fires its EV_BLESSING once; the handler calls GainPermStati directly for
#   all nine maladies, the same call lib/religion.irh:5958 (Zurvash) makes.
#   No ThrowEff, no scripted spell throw: GainPermStati is not the spell, it
#   is a shortcut to the AFFLICTION only, so that the CURE below is still the
#   real thing, cast by the player.
#
#   Half two, THE CURE: wizard "Learn Any Spell" teaches "Heal;spell"
#   (lib/pspells.irh's Priest / Scroll Spell) as an innate ability, then
#   [u] Innate Heal, ENTER casts it on the default target -- himself. An
#   innate cast always succeeds (Character::SpellRating returns 100 for
#   SP_INNATE, src/Magic.cpp:3188-3191) and costs no mana. This is the same
#   route tools/keys/heal-maladies.keys used for poison alone before this
#   widening, and reused unchanged.
#
# THE ORACLE: wizard "Examine Player Data" (Player::Dump, src/Debug.cpp)
# prints an unfiltered "Stati (n):" list naming every active status by its
# full constant name via STATI_CONSTNAMES (src/Tables.cpp) -- unlike the
# right-hand status panel, which shows at most one malady at a time behind an
# if/else-if priority chain (src/Term.cpp:426-444) and never mentions HALLU,
# BLEEDING, CHOKING or WOUNDED at all. The dump scrolls; ten DOWN presses
# were measured (tools/fixtures/heal-maladies-god.irh's own header run) to
# bring the whole nine-entry block on screen from a fresh, top-scrolled
# entry, both before and after the cure, because entering the screen calls
# ClearScroll(true) each time and resets the scroll position. Do NOT scroll
# further: past the end of Player::Dump's content, this debug view's
# scroller segfaults (observed 2026-09-17, unrelated to any of the nine
# maladies -- reproduced by continuing to press DOWN after the last line of
# output already showed. Not filed: src/ is off limits for this bead and the
# view is a wizard/debug tool, not player-facing).
#
# WHY NOT THE STATUS PANEL: it is a single priority-ordered line (Paralyzed >
# Poisoned > Diseased > Stunned > Sickly > Confused > Blind), so afflicting
# all nine at once would only ever show ONE name there, and it structurally
# cannot show HALLU, BLEEDING, CHOKING or WOUNDED under any affliction.
#
# EMPIRICAL RESULT ON THE BLOCKING-MALADY TRAP: tried, not assumed. One
# single run affects the player with all nine simultaneously -- including
# STUNNED, CONFUSED and BLIND -- then teaches and casts Heal in the same run
# with no split needed. The wizard-mode menu commands and the innate cast
# both went through untouched: HP stayed 42/42 across the run (no bleed or
# choke damage: the fixture pins Val/Mag to 0), the cast produced "You feel
# fully refreshed!", and the after-dump showed all nine gone. Nothing here
# forced a per-malady run.

@include chargen.keys

w
y                       # Enter wizard mode? [yn] -- only asked once
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Heal Maladies Test God" ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10                # scroll the debug dump down to the Stati block
@dump:control
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Heal;spell" ENTER

u
@choose "Innate Heal"
ENTER                   # confirm the default target: self

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10                # same fixed scroll: ClearScroll(true) reset it to top
@dump:after
ESC

@quit
